{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Local logs persist across node1 restarts and logging recovers afterward.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A pre-restart marker was durably recorded with journald healthy, the reboot was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, and node1 returned running with journald active. The pre-restart marker remained readable, a new marker was recorded, both boots were listed, and journal integrity passed. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently confirm the reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-73a94023513145ec","cmd-be15ea51a56648a1","cmd-97286cd452b54a3f","cmd-4b246bccdde64a69","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Local logs have a 14-day retention policy.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The journald drop-in sets MaxRetentionSec=14day, the corresponding vacuum was applied, and the effective configuration still reported the 14-day policy after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8077e8f11fdd42f3","cmd-82b8a5e18406405b","cmd-ec2fc97c22d84f54","cmd-4b246bccdde64a69"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Local logging has bounded disk growth.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective persistent policy limits journal use to 512M, preserves 1G of free space, and limits individual files to 64M. After restart, journald directly reported a 512M system-journal maximum while current usage was 10.6M.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8077e8f11fdd42f3","cmd-ec2fc97c22d84f54","cmd-4b246bccdde64a69","cmd-ea4e4588b30a4c1a"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating the drop-in and persistent journal directory established the requested policy; restarting, flushing, rotating, and vacuuming applied it; marker writes collected bounded persistence evidence; and the scheduled reboot fulfilled both the task's restart behavior test and the provider restart protocol. Post-executor observations show no failed services, unchanged listening endpoints aside from expected process-ID changes, healthy package state, and only normal reboot-regenerated systemd private directories. The restart protocol is complete and agrees with the fixed boot-identity observations.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8077e8f11fdd42f3","cmd-82b8a5e18406405b","cmd-73a94023513145ec","cmd-be15ea51a56648a1","cmd-4b246bccdde64a69","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Persistent journald storage survived an observed reboot, the effective 14-day retention policy remained active afterward, and journald recognized and enforced a 512M runtime maximum. The mandatory node-restart evidence protocol is complete and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":["The evidence does not span a full 14-day aging interval or fill the journal to its 512M limit; long-horizon expiration and pressure-driven pruning therefore rely on the directly observed effective journald policy and runtime-reported maximum rather than a prolonged stress test."]}
